                                    <h1>Onam Marketing Playbook for D2C Brands (Kerala) 2026-2027</h1>
                                    <p>Onam (August-September, dates vary annually) is Kerala's biggest festival — 10-day celebration + Sadya (traditional feast) + Kasavu (traditional white + gold textile) + gifting + family-visiting. Drives 20-35% of Q3 revenue for Kerala + Malayali diaspora-focused D2C brands. Here is the complete playbook.</p>
                                    <h2>Onam Timeline</h2>
                                    <p>Onam is 10-day festival (Atham to Thiruvonam). Peak day Thiruvonam typically in September.<br><strong>4-6 weeks before Onam:</strong> creative + inventory + Kasavu textile prep.<br><strong>2-3 weeks before Thiruvonam:</strong> full campaign launch.<br><strong>Onam 10-day period:</strong> daily celebration content + peak purchase.<br><strong>Peak Thiruvonam day:</strong> celebration + Sadya + family.<br><strong>Post-Onam:</strong> follow-through + retention flows.</p>
                                    <h2>Category-Specific Onam Playbook</h2>
                                    <p><strong>Kasavu + traditional textile:</strong> Kasavu saree + Kasavu mundu + traditional white + gold textile peaks. Category-defining Onam product.<br><strong>Sadya + F&amp;B:</strong> Traditional feast ingredients + banana leaf + specialty foods.<br><strong>Jewelry + gold:</strong> Wedding + gifting purchases.<br><strong>Kerala-heritage brands:</strong> Ayurveda + spice + specialty Kerala products.<br><strong>Home + flowers:</strong> Pookalam (flower arrangement) + home decoration.<br><strong>Gifting hampers:</strong> Onam gifting to family + colleagues + relatives.</p>
                                    <h2>Regional Reach + Diaspora</h2>
                                    <p><strong>Kerala primary market:</strong> Onam-native audience.<br><strong>Malayali diaspora:</strong> Gulf + USA + UK + Australia + Singapore + Canada. 3M+ global Malayali audience celebrates.<br><strong>UAE + Gulf Malayali:</strong> Largest Malayali diaspora market. Onam major event for Gulf Malayalis.<br><strong>USA + UK Malayali:</strong> Association-driven Onam celebrations + gifting.<br>Diaspora Onam is meaningful revenue segment for Kerala-heritage brands.</p>
                                    <h2>Cultural Sensitivity + Authenticity</h2>
                                    <p>Onam requires cultural authenticity — Malayalam content + Kerala traditions + Malayali cultural references. Non-Malayali brands attempting Onam campaigns without cultural depth backfire.<br><strong>Best practice:</strong> genuine Malayalam content + Kerala tradition celebration + Malayali cultural references + partnership with Kerala creators + authentic Onam-related product offerings.</p>
                                    <h2>Ad Budget Concentration</h2>
                                    <p>Onam CPM inflation in Kerala: 40-70% peak 2 weeks. Malayalam-language content essential.<br><strong>Recommended allocation:</strong> pre-Onam (4-6 weeks): 25-30%. Peak Onam 10-day period: 55-65%. Post-Onam: 10-20%.<br>Multi-country Malayali diaspora targeting requires regional-specific creative + cultural adaptation.</p>

