                                    <div class="faq-section" style="margin-top:40px;">
                                        <h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
                                        <h3>Should non-Malayali brands do Onam campaigns?</h3>
                                        <p>Only with cultural depth + Malayalam content + genuine celebration positioning. Superficial Onam-branding backfires. Best for brands with genuine Kerala / Malayali connection.</p>
                                        <h3>How big is Malayali diaspora Onam market?</h3>
                                        <p>3M+ global Malayali audience. Gulf + USA + UK + Australia + Canada + Singapore. Meaningful revenue segment for Kerala-heritage brands.</p>
                                        <h3>What is Kasavu?</h3>
                                        <p>Traditional Kerala white cotton textile with gold border. Category-defining Onam textile purchase for saree + mundu. Cultural + festival requirement.</p>
                                        <h3>Is Onam bigger than Diwali for Kerala brands?</h3>
                                        <p>For Kerala + Malayali-focused brands: yes. Onam is Kerala's biggest festival — 20-35% of Q3 revenue. Diwali less prominent in Kerala than North India.</p>
